# Test-suite registry and runner — Design Spec
S1. **Status:** Design approved in brainstorming on 2026-10-18.
S2. Next step: an implementation plan from the writing-plans skill (`entry_check.py` reported plan id 54 as next free on 2026-10-18).

## What this builds
S3. A registry of the repo's directory-scoped pytest suites, a runner that reads it, and a commit lint that keeps it complete:
S4. - `build/suites.toml` holds one entry per suite: its directory, its `--with` deps, the extra deps that unlock its skips, its interpreters, and its notes.
S5. - `build/run_suites.py` (stdlib only) lists the suites, runs one or more of them, runs all of them, and checks the registry.
S6. - `run_suites.py --check` becomes the ninth commit lint.
S7. It fails when a directory that holds tests is not registered.
S8. The root `CLAUDE.md` then replaces its per-suite commands with a short block that points at the runner.

## Why
S9. - **The 200-line limit.** The `claude-md-size` check (a commit lint, through `build/check_conformance.py`) fails at 200 lines.
S10. `CLAUDE.md` had 199 on `main` at `456e3fb`.
S11. Its Commands block spends lines 66–125, 60 lines, on one `cd <dir> && uv run … python -m pytest -q` command and comment per suite.
S12. Each new suite costs two or three more lines.
S13. - **Three plans competed for the last lines on 2026-10-18.** Plan 50 (the superpowers upstream fixes, lowmason/agent-skills#56) took the file from 195 to 199.
S14. Plan 52 (the write-with-asd-ste100 skill, not merged) needs two more lines.
S15. Its open question Q4 asked where they come from: (a) fold seven suites under one comment, (b) record a size deviation, or (c) move the per-suite commands out of the root file first.
S16. This spec is option (c).
S17. - **Plan 38 fixed the same problem once.** In plan 38, Task 2 condensed `CLAUDE.md` from 224 lines to 170 and kept every command in place.
S18. The file then grew back to 199 by 2026-10-18.
S19. A registry removes the per-suite growth.
S20. - **Compound commands.** Worktree-isolated sessions and their subagents have refused compound shell such as `cd X && Y` (seen on 2026-10-12).
S21. A runner gives each suite a single simple command.

## Decisions taken in brainstorming
S22. The owner took these decisions on 2026-10-18.
S23. Each records the option that the owner chose.
S24. 1. **The coverage guard is a ninth commit lint:** "`run_suites.py --check` joins build/run_commit_lints.sh, so the pre-commit hook and CI run it."
S25. 2. **Plan 52's Q4 is (c):** "This work lands whole, registry and CLAUDE.md shrink, ahead of plan 52's Task 6.
S26. Task 6 then adds one build/suites.toml entry instead of editing Commands.
S27. Plan 52's planning session amends its plan to match and records Q4 as (c)."
S28. 3. **Approach A:** "build/suites.toml (data) + build/run_suites.py (stdlib, tomllib).
S29. Matches conformance.toml and manifest.toml.
S30. One central file, sorted by name."
S31. Rejected: a Python list inside the runner (every suite change becomes a code edit), and one manifest per suite directory (`install.py` copies skill directories, so the manifests would ship with installed skills).
S32. An `@`-imported document was ruled out before the vote: the guide says imported files load at launch too, so it only moves lines.
S33. 4. **Design section 1** (the registry keys and the runner's behaviour) was approved as presented.
S34. It is R1–R3 below.
S35. 5. **Design section 2** (the guard, the file edits, the tests and the couplings) was approved as presented.
S36. It is R4–R7 below.

### R1 — Scope
S37. R1.1 The registry holds every **directory suite**: a directory where pytest runs as a whole, with no selection argument.
S38. On `main` at `456e3fb` there are 18: the 17 in `CLAUDE.md` lines 66–125, and `build/cc_guide`, whose command is line 145.
S39. R1.2 These commands **stay literal in `CLAUDE.md`**.
S40. They are selections or tools, not directory suites, and their comments say when to run them:
S41. - `test_runtime_support.py` (lines 63–64), `test_commit_lints.py`, the `-k declared_dependencies` and `-k test_real_skill` lints, `test_check_jax_examples.py`, and the "Single test" example;
S42. - the commit lints, the snippet tiers, the JAX CPU examples, the smoke test, the two `build.py` rebuilds, `verify_citations.py`, `extract_structure.py`, and `cli.py lint` and `check`.
S43. R1.3 `build/run_commit_lints.sh` keeps its literal commands.
S44. It does not call the runner, except for the new `--check` lint (R4).

### R2 — The registry: `build/suites.toml`
S45. R2.1 One `[[suite]]` table per directory suite, sorted by `name`.
S46. A header comment states the keys, the sort order, and that the ninth commit lint checks the file.
S47. R2.2 Keys:
S48. | Key | Type | Required | Meaning |
S49. | `name` | string | yes | The name that the runner takes. A skill's suite uses the skill's name; the others are `build`, `cc-guide` and `hooks`. |
S50. | `dir` | string | yes | The repo-relative directory that pytest runs from. |
S51. | `with` | list of strings | yes | The default `--with` deps, in the order the current command gives them. It includes `pytest`. |
S52. | `extras` | list of strings | no | The deps that unlock skips. Only `--extras` adds them. |
S53. | `pythons` | list of strings | no | The interpreters, one run each, in order. Default `['3.13']`. |
S54. | `notes` | list of strings | no | What the suite covers or needs: opt-in environment variables, expected warnings, run times, why some tests skip or fail. |
S55. R2.3 The entries carry the text of today's commands and comments.
S56. Every command, dependency and note survives; the only change is the form.
S57. The inventory, from `CLAUDE.md` at `456e3fb`:
S58. | `name` | `dir` | `with` (after `pytest`) | `extras` | `pythons` |
S59. | `bayesian-workflow` | `skills/bayesian-workflow/scripts` | arviz, arviz-stats, numpy, xarray | matplotlib | default |
S60. | `brainstorming` | `skills/brainstorming/scripts` | — | — | default |
S61. | `build` | `build` | numpy, polars, pyyaml | arviz>=1.0, arviz-base, arviz-stats, arviz-plots, numpyro, jax, matplotlib | default |
S62. | `cc-guide` | `build/cc_guide` | — | — | default |
S63. | `classification-codes` | `skills/classification-codes/scripts` | polars | — | default |
S64. | `describe-critique-methodology` | `skills/describe-critique-methodology/scripts` | — | — | default |
S65. | `design-architecture` | `skills/design-architecture/scripts` | — | — | default |
S66. | `explore-data` | `skills/explore-data/scripts` | polars | — | default |
S67. | `geographic-codes` | `skills/geographic-codes/scripts` | polars, fastexcel | — | default |
S68. | `hooks` | `hooks` | — | — | 3.13, /usr/bin/python3 |
S69. | `llm-wiki` | `skills/llm-wiki/scripts` | — | — | default |
S70. | `recommend-probabilistic-model` | `skills/recommend-probabilistic-model/scripts` | numpy, polars | — | default |
S71. | `recommend-visualization` | `skills/recommend-visualization/scripts` | numpy, polars | — | default |
S72. | `subagent-driven-development` | `skills/subagent-driven-development/scripts` | — | — | default |
S73. | `systematic-debugging` | `skills/systematic-debugging` | — | — | default |
S74. | `track-model-experiments` | `skills/track-model-experiments/scripts` | numpy, polars, arviz, numpyro, h5netcdf, h5py | — | default |
S75. | `tune-hyperparameters` | `skills/tune-hyperparameters/scripts` | numpy, polars | scikit-learn, optuna | default |
S76. | `writing-plans` | `skills/writing-plans/scripts` | — | — | default |
S77. The notes carry the rest of each comment.
S78. Examples: `build`'s missing `build/.scratch/` in a fresh clone or worktree; `bayesian-workflow`'s `CALIBRATION_SWEEP=1` sweep and its expected arviz warnings; `llm-wiki`'s `@needs_pilot` tests and `$LLM_WIKI_ROOT`; `brainstorming`'s node skip; `tune-hyperparameters`' "`--with sklearn` fails"; `track-model-experiments`' run time; the guard's 3.9 floor, its launchd-PATH skips and its Gate B probe for `hooks`.

### R3 — The runner: `build/run_suites.py`
S79. R3.1 Stdlib only (`tomllib`, `argparse`, `subprocess`, `shlex`), Python 3.13.
S80. Invoked as `uv run --python 3.13 python build/run_suites.py …` from any directory.
S81. It finds the repo root from its own path, never from the working directory.
S82. R3.2 **One run** is one interpreter of one suite.
S83. Its command is `uv run --python <python> --with <dep> … python -m pytest -q [<args>]`, run with the suite's `dir` as its working directory.
S84. Its shell form is `cd <dir> && <command>`, with shell quoting where a word needs it.
S85. With default options, the shell form equals the suite's current `CLAUDE.md` command, character for character.
S86. For `hooks`, whose line chains two runs as `cd hooks && A && B`, the two shell forms are `cd hooks && A` and `cd hooks && B`.
S87. R3.3 **`--list [NAME …]`** prints, for each named suite (default: all): its name and directory, the shell form of each run, its extras, and its notes.
S88. `--extras` and the `--` arguments apply here too, so `--list` prints the exact command that a run would use.
S89. R3.4 **`NAME [NAME …]`** runs the named suites, in the order given, one run per interpreter in `pythons`.
S90. Each run starts with a `== <name> (<python>)` header, and the suite's notes follow its first run's header.
S91. Then pytest's output streams.
S92. A failed run does not stop the next one.
S93. R3.5 **`--extras`** adds each suite's `extras` after its `with` deps.
S94. Arguments after **`--`** go to pytest (a test node ID, `-k`, `-s`, `-rs`) in every run.
S95. R3.6 **`--all`** runs every suite except one whose `dir` lies inside another suite's `dir`.
S96. Today that is `cc-guide`: `cd build && pytest` collects `build/cc_guide` already.
S97. `--all` prints one line for each suite that it skips.
S98. A suite named on the command line always runs.
S99. R3.7 **Exit status:** 0 when every run exits 0; 1 when any run fails (pytest's exit 5, no tests collected, counts as a failure); 2 for a usage error, an unknown suite name, or a registry that fails validation.
S100. The last line names the failed runs, or says that every run passed.
S101. A run whose `uv` cannot start counts as failed.
S102. R3.8 The runner passes its environment to every run unchanged.
S103. `CALIBRATION_SWEEP=1 uv run --python 3.13 python build/run_suites.py bayesian-workflow -- -s` therefore runs the sweep.
S104. R3.9 Validation fails closed.
S105. An unknown key, a missing required key, a wrong type, a duplicate name or directory, or a `with` list without `pytest` stops `--list`, a named run and `--all` with exit 2.
S106. `--check` reports the same failures as findings (R4.3).
S107. A misspelled key can therefore never run a suite without its deps.

### R4 — The guard: `run_suites.py --check`
S108. R4.1 `--check` reports two kinds of findings:
S109. - **registry:** R3.9's validation, plus a registered `dir` that does not exist or holds no pytest file;
S110. - **coverage:** a directory that holds a pytest file (`test_*.py` or `*_test.py`, pytest's default patterns) and does not lie inside any registered `dir`.
S111. R4.2 The file list is `git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard`, run at the repo root.
S112. Ignored trees, `.claude/worktrees/` and `build/.scratch/` among them, drop out.
S113. Untracked new suites count, as the hook's other lints read untracked drafts too.
S114. If git fails, `--check` fails.
S115. R4.3 Output: `suite registry ok` and exit 0, or one line per finding and exit 1.
S116. R4.4 `build/run_commit_lints.sh` runs it as the ninth lint, named `suite_registry`: `run suite_registry uv run --python 3.13 python build/run_suites.py --check`.
S117. Its header says "nine".

